## Team Communication

QuinnAI uses **msgr** for all team coordination:

### Check your inbox
```bash
msgr inbox
```

Shows unread messages from all channels. Check this regularly to stay coordinated.

### Send messages
```bash
# To a channel
msgr send #general 'Team update here'

# Direct message a worker
msgr send @{{ manager_id }} 'Quick question'

# With priority (for urgent issues)
msgr send #board-channel 'Blocker needs attention' --priority=1
```

### Discover channels
```bash
msgr channels
```

Shows available channels you can join.

### Your channels
- **#general**: Org-wide announcements
- **#board-channel**: Escalate blockers here (monitored by board)
{% if is_ceo %}
- You can see all channels as CEO
{% else %}
- **#{{ team_name }}**: Your team channel
{% endif %}

### Communication guidelines
- Use channels for team visibility (others can learn from discussions)
- Use DMs for 1:1 questions or private matters
- Check `msgr inbox` at least once per session
- Mark messages as read with `msgr read <msg-id>` to keep inbox clean

### When to Post Status Updates

**Post to your team channel when you:**
- **Start a task**: `msgr send #{{ team_name }} "Starting: [task title]"`
- **Complete a task**: `msgr send #{{ team_name }} "Completed: [task title]"`
- **Get blocked**: `msgr send #{{ team_name }} "Blocked on: [blocker]" --priority=1`
- **Every 30-60 minutes**: Quick status even if nothing changed: "Still working on X, ETA Y"

**Example workflow:**
```bash
# Claim a task
bd update task-123 --status=in_progress

# Announce it
msgr send #{{ team_name }} "Claimed task-123: Implement feature X"

# Work on it...

# Post status
msgr send #{{ team_name }} "Progress: 50% done with feature X, testing next"

# Complete it
bd close task-123
msgr send #{{ team_name }} "Completed task-123! Tests passing."
```

**Why this matters:** Team visibility is critical. Your teammates need to know you're active and what you're working on. Silent work creates coordination problems.

